 **Humane Disposal:** Some clinics will simply handle the disposal of the body for a very small fee.\n\n### 4. Municipal Waste / Trash Disposal\nIf you have no other options, most municipal waste services allow small pets to be placed in the regular household trash. \n* Wrap the body securely in paper towels or a cloth, place it inside a sealed plastic bag, and place it into your outside trash bin as close to collection day as possible. \n* Check your local municipal guidelines first, as rules vary by city.\n\n---\n\n**What to do in the meantime:**\nIf you cannot bury or take your hamster to the vet immediately, wrap the body in a soft cloth, place it inside a sealed plastic bag or container, and store it in a cool, dry place. If it will be more than a few hours, placing it in a refrigerator or freezer will preserve the body safely until you are ready.",
